        "keyideas": "The Pacific Railway Act (1862) funded two companies — the Central Pacific (building east from Sacramento, largely with 10,000+ Chinese laborers) and the Union Pacific (building west from Omaha, largely with Irish, German, and Italian immigrants). They met at Promontory Summit, Utah, on May 10, 1869. Travel fell from months to about a week. The benefits (faster trade, western settlement) came with heavy costs to Native nations and the bison, and hard, dangerous, underpaid work for immigrant laborers.",
